.TH GIT-ROOST 1 "2026-07-31" "git-roost 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git\-roost \- top for git, across every repo and worktree on the box
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git\-roost
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git\-roost
shows every git working tree it can find in one table, grouped by what it costs
to ignore: trees stuck part\-way through a rebase or merge first, then diverged
trees, then uncommitted work, then unpushed commits, then trees that have fallen
behind.
.PP
It is a companion to
.BR roost (1),
which reports on Claude Code sessions. Sessions report what they intend to do;
git reports what actually happened.
.PP
.B git\-roost
is read\-only by construction: every git invocation is checked against a
whitelist of read\-only plumbing subcommands and raises otherwise, so the tool
cannot modify a working tree, an index or a ref.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch " [\fISECS\fR]"
Redraw every \fISECS\fR seconds, default 3.
.TP
.BR \-\-log " [\fIN\fR]"
Show a commit feed merged across every repository, newest first, default 25
entries. Commits are deduplicated per repository, so a repo and its worktrees do
not each contribute a copy.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Expand the collapsed QUIET group.
.TP
.BR \-\-root " \fIDIR\fR"
Where to look for repositories. Repeatable. Defaults to ~/GitHub.
.TP
.BR \-\-depth " \fIN\fR"
How deep to search below each root, default 3. Worktrees kept beside a repo live
at <root>/.worktrees/<repo>/<slug>, which is depth 3.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the collected records as JSON rather than a table.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colour output.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH COLUMNS
.TP
.B WORK
Uncommitted work: \fBclean\fR, a count of tracked changes, \fB+N?\fR untracked,
or both. Untracked files are marked but never promoted to the UNCOMMITTED group.
.TP
.B DRIFT
Position against the base branch: \fB=\fR in sync, \fB^N\fR ahead, \fBvN\fR
behind, \fB^NvM\fR diverged, \fB\-\fR unknown. A dash means unknown, never in
sync.
.TP
.B STASH
Number of stash entries, blank when there are none.
.TP
.B LAST
Age of the most recent commit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_WORKERS
Size of the thread pool used to scan trees. Default 12.
.TP
.B GIT_ROOST_TIMEOUT
Seconds before an individual git call is abandoned. Default 5.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, colour output is disabled. See https://no-color.org.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, including when no repositories are found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR roost (1),
.BR git\-status (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
.SH AUTHOR
George M. Howard <dev@swamplink.com>
